`styled-ppx.generate` writes the twin selectors (`_t1_`, `_t2_`) only for an
atom that has a competitor in the same input: another atom of that input
that overlaps it, that it does not replace, and that the sheet order may put
after it. The names below have the
real class format (context, family, mask, value), because the competitor
test reads them.

`same.ml` holds an `@media` `padding` and a base `padding-top`: each is the
other's competitor, but the sheet puts the `@media` rule after the base one,
so only the base `padding-top` gets twin selectors. `first.ml` and `second.ml`
hold the same pair apart: no input has a competitor, so both stay plain.
`alone.ml` holds two atoms of different properties: plain too. The `:hover`
atom of `same.ml` is of another kind (a selector context), so it is no
competitor of the plain ones.

  $ cat > same.ml <<EOF
  > [@@@css "._a_940008kzem{padding-top:12px;}"]
  > [@@@css "@media (max-width:1200px){._a_0p2f09462m4{padding:11px;}}"]
  > [@@@css "._a_qyw7u940008dvpz:hover{padding-top:13px;}"]
  > EOF

  $ cat > first.ml <<EOF
  > [@@@css "@media (max-width:1200px){._a_0p2f094kf94{padding:21px;}}"]
  > EOF

  $ cat > second.ml <<EOF
  > [@@@css "._a_940008xfx1{padding-top:22px;}"]
  > EOF

  $ cat > alone.ml <<EOF
  > [@@@css "._a_4eanme{color:red;}"]
  > [@@@css "._a_39004tydx{background-color:blue;}"]
  > EOF

  $ styled-ppx.generate --order source same.ml first.ml second.ml alone.ml
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  ._a_4eanme{color:red;}
  ._a_940008kzem,._t1_940008kzem:not(x-),._t2_940008kzem:not(x-):not(x-){padding-top:12px;}
  ._a_940008xfx1{padding-top:22px;}
  ._a_39004tydx{background-color:blue;}
  @media (max-width:1200px){._a_0p2f09462m4{padding:11px;}}
  @media (max-width:1200px){._a_0p2f094kf94{padding:21px;}}
  ._a_qyw7u940008dvpz:hover{padding-top:13px;}
